>dwivian@ada.stat.uga.edu (Dwivian Unterschreiber) writes:

>how should I go about uncursing HUGE quantities of items (found a ghost
>level, killed off all the ghosts, and now have a pile of cursed stuff
>that would be fine if it wasn't cursed)?  I know that a blessed remove
>curse scroll will remove the curse from all items in your pack, but
>what about stuff you aren't carrying?

SPOILERS FOLLOW!!


















  I assume you're familiar with the other common ways of uncursing
items, e.g. dipping in a fountain, prayer, and holy water.
You can uncurse a large pile by zapping with a wand of cancellation
(but you lose the enchantment) so this option is not too good for
scrolls, potions or wands. But my favorite way to uncurse large
numbers of items is to let a lich do it. This method works best for
high level characters since one needs magic and cold resistance.
Drop or take off all non-essential items, wear only a magic resistance
cloak or gray dragon scale, keep your weapon (just in case).
Pick up all the cursed items you can and walk up to a lich. He won't
be able to hurt you if you have the above-mentioned intrinsics.
Let him attack you and every so often you get the 'malignant aura'
message that indicates you've been cursed. Cursing a cursed item causes
it to become uncursed. Drop each item as it is uncursed. Eventually
you can uncurse everything as well as any originally uncursed
items which the lich curses. This can also be done with a titan or
golden naga but these monsters also do significant damage so be
careful. The only danger is that lichs (especially master and demi)
can summon monsters on occasion. For this reason it's useful to have
teleport capability. Lichs are generally so annoying and useless
that this tactic is particularly satisfying.

